	•	Section 2 Comments/Quotes: The investigators identified 66,590 lung transplant records, excluded recipients with a documented pretransplant malignancy, leaving 38,788, and then excluded those lost to follow-up, producing a final cohort of 30,917 recipients. Twenty-five percent developed a post-transplant malignancy. Figure 2 reports 43% female and presents ethnicity and age distributions, but an overall mean age was not reported. The registry variables included demographics, HLA/PRA, serology, donor characteristics, laboratory values, transplantation details, hospital course, rejection, survival, and other complications.

