	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: Gradient Boosting was compared with Random Forest, Decision Tree, LARS, Neural Network, logistic regression, rule induction, and SVM. The dataset was divided into 70% training and 30% testing. Medical experts reviewed 544 candidate variables and excluded 173 because of irrelevance, redundancy, excessive missingness above 30%, or excessive correlation. Gradient Boosting variable-importance rankings were used for interpretation. Reported model settings included shrinkage 0.1, 50 iterations, and use of 60% of observations for fitting individual boosted trees.

