	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The target was occurrence of de novo malignant cancer after lung transplantation among recipients with no prior malignancy. In the held-out test set, Gradient Boosting achieved AUC 0.746, accuracy 0.690, sensitivity 0.731, specificity 0.649, and precision 0.676. No AUC confidence interval, NPV, or F1-score was reported. The study did not report formal calibration assessment or decision-curve analysis.

